**You need:** an [exam](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-create-an-exam) that already exists, and access to
the class.

## Steps

1. Open **Exams** and select the exam.
2. Pick the **class** from the class list.
3. Select **Add Results**.
4. At the top, choose the **subject** and the **teacher** the marks are credited to.
5. Type marks down the list of students. As you go, the counters at the top of the screen keep
   score: **_n_ of _total_ entered**, and **_n_ absent**.
6. For students who did not sit the paper, tick **Absent** rather than entering `0`. A zero is a
   mark and drags averages down; absent is excluded from them.
7. When everyone who sat is entered, use **Mark remaining absent** to tick the stragglers in one go
   — but read the entered/absent counts first and make sure the remainder really are absentees and
   not people you forgot.
8. Select **Save Results** and confirm.

## Changing a mark afterwards

Saved marks are not freely editable. Editing one raises a **change request** with an optional note,
which someone with approval rights reviews under **Exams → Result Changes**. This is deliberate —
it leaves a trail on marks that have already been seen.

If you get **The mark has moved** while editing, someone else changed that mark after you opened the
screen. Reload and look at the current value before re-submitting; your change was not applied.

